{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1nWiaAzVZsEJXHfqjSr", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I had to stop before finishing the sweep. The device connection broke (every device call now returns `BrokenPipeError`, including `observe`, `screenshot`, `wait` and `open_app`), so I could not continue. I have **not** signed off, and I have filed **no reports**, because I did not reproduce a bug I could confirm.\n\n**What I checked (no defects confirmed):**\n- **Card browser:** search `deck:Spanish` shows 5 cards and, after switching to notes, 5 notes. Cards/notes toggle keeps its columns (Cards: Sort Field / Card Type / Due / Deck; Notes: Sort Field / Note Type / Cards / Tags) and its count label (\"7 cards shown\" / \"7 notes shown\"). Notes mode persists across navigation and an app restart. Rotation keeps the search and the mode. Undo \"Update Note\" reverts the edit.\n- **Deck list:** arrows show `>` when collapsed and `v` when expanded. Collapse and expand of Spanish and Ben hide and show their children. The state survives HOME and relaunch. Counts (French 3, Spanish 5, 8 due) agree with the browser.\n- **Add note / edit note:** an empty Front is rejected with \"The first field is empty.\" A new note saves into the chosen deck and appears in the browser. Editing persists. Leaving the editor with changes asks \"Discard changes?\", and Discard keeps the original value.\n- **Deck chooser sort:** decks appear as Ben, Ben::Zed, French, Spanish, Spanish::Verbs. This is consistent with sorting by full nested name.\n\n**Not finished:**\n- Adding a note to Spanish::Verbs, then checking that the Deck column, the `deck:Spanish` count and the deck list all agree on the nested deck.\n- Truncate-content behaviour per mode, and case or edge-case sorting in the deck chooser.\n- Rotation and relaunch checks on the deck list and the chooser.\n\n**Possible issue I did not file:** after I created `French::Gram`, the parent `French` showed a collapsed arrow and hid its child. Ben and Spanish also show collapsed when their child was created. I could not tell whether this is intended for this build, so it needs a decision before it becomes a report.\n\n**Changes I made to the test data:**\n- Created decks `Spanish::Verbs`, `Ben::Zed` and `French::Gram`.\n- Added a note \"gato / cat\" to Spanish.\n- Edited the Back of \"gato\" to \"cat (feline)\", then undid that edit, so it reads \"cat\" again.\n- Changed the collapsed state of Spanish, Ben and French.\n\nIf you can restore the device connection, I can pick up from the unfinished items above. Otherwise, the sweep is incomplete and should not be treated as a PASS."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 336, "cache_read_input_tokens": 333866, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 336}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f4f90d2b-c09e-4b03-b144-2f5d9c18860c", "uuid": "dcf3b546-378f-48c4-815f-c988c0a87475", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T23:21:17.469Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1nWiKnbANE3G12pyfYw"}
